NNAAMMEE
     mmkkaalliiaass — a YP map conversion program

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     mmkkaalliiaass [--nnvv] [--EE | --ee [--dduu]] _i_n_p_u_t [_o_u_t_p_u_t]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     mmkkaalliiaass is used to convert a mail.aliases map to a mail.byaddr map.  This
     is an inverse map of user@host (or user!host) back to alias.

     The options are as follows:

     --dd      Assume domain names are OK.  Only useful together with --EE or --ee.

     --EE      Same as --ee, but also check for any MX-record.

     --ee      Check host to verify that it exists.

     --nn      Capitalize name. e.g., mats.o.jansson becomes Mats.O.Jansson.

     --uu      Assume UUCP names are OK.  Only useful together with --EE or --ee.

     --vv      Verbose mode.

     _i_n_p_u_t   Use this map as input.

     _o_u_t_p_u_t  Use this map as output.  If the output map isn't given, don't
             create database.  Can be useful together with --EE or --ee.

